  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760341,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1k-Mini-Bdash for Commodore 64: A Tiny Triumph of Skill!\n\nPrepare for a surprisingly addictive and challenging miniature golf experience in *1k-Mini-Bdash*, a remarkably compact game squeezed into just 1 kilobyte for the Commodore 64! Don't let the small size fool you; this isn't your average putt-putt. \n\nNavigate a series of cleverly designed, increasingly difficult holes, relying on precision and timing to sink your ball. The game features a unique, minimalist aesthetic, emphasizing gameplay over flashy graphics.  Each hole presents a new puzzle, demanding careful consideration of angles, speed, and the subtle physics of the ball. \n\nMaster the art of bank shots, utilize ramps, and avoid obstacles to achieve par.  *1k-Mini-Bdash* is a testament to the ingenuity of Commodore 64 programmers, offering a compelling and rewarding experience in a truly tiny package.  Can you conquer all the holes and become a miniature golf master?  A true test of skill and a fascinating glimpse into the limitations – and creativity – of early home computing!"
    },
